<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiberias</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiberias is a city on the western shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-galilee">Sea of Galilee</a> in northern Israel. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-antipas">Herod Antipas</a> around 19 CE and named after the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a>, it became his capital and later a leading centre of Jewish scholarship, where much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> Talmud was compiled. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of the crusader Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiberias.jpg" alt="Tiberias" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: דוידי ורדי · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:92250_tiberias_PikiWiki_Israel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
